#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# random_variate

#% text
# `random_variate(d)` gives a random value drawn from the distribution `d`.

#% text
# `random_variate(d, n)` gives a list of `n` values; `random_variate(d, [n1, n2, ...])` gives nested lists.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The values come from the session's generator; `seed(k)` makes them repeatable.

#% item
# Continuous distributions give machine reals; discrete ones give integers.

#% item
# The parameters of the distribution must be numbers.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A standard normal value:

#% cell
seed(1); random_variate(normal_distribution())
#% output
#= -0.8289777865469348

#% text
# Five values with mean 10 and standard deviation 2:

#% cell
random_variate(normal_distribution(10, 2), 5)
#% output
#= [13.075859784335181, 10.867251516087766, 10.820685436010395, 10.444509280480991, 7.365381201635947]

#% text
# Counts from a Poisson distribution:

#% cell
random_variate(poisson_distribution(3), 10)
#% output
#= [2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 3, 1, 1, 2, 1]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A 2 x 3 array of uniform values:

#% cell
random_variate(uniform_distribution([0, 1]), [2, 3])
#% output
#= [[0.44115230692063645, 0.7526692246241176, 0.6523591909068733], [0.21820093829849596, 0.017459750127277407, 0.8185179936332682]]

#% text
# Binomial counts:

#% cell
random_variate(binomial_distribution(10, 0.3), 8)
#% output
#= [2, 2, 2, 5, 3, 1, 4, 5]

#% text
# Gamma values:

#% cell
random_variate(gamma_distribution(2, 3), 3)
#% output
#= [3.857570110538446, 0.4667213221212127, 7.992416333910114]

#% text
# A histogram of many normal values:

#% cell
seed(2); histogram(random_variate(normal_distribution(), 2000))
#% output
#= image("random_variate.files/random_variate-7.svgz")

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# A random walk in the plane with Gaussian steps of width 0.15, the proposal step of a Metropolis sampler:

#% cell
seed(11); walk = nest_list(p => p + 0.15*random_variate(normal_distribution(), 2), [0, 0], 500); list_line_plot(walk)
#% output
#= image("random_variate.files/random_variate-8.svgz")

#% text
# Fit a distribution to simulated data:

#% cell
seed(3); estimated_distribution(random_variate(normal_distribution(5, 2), 1000), normal_distribution(m, s))
#% output
#= normal_distribution(5.041948397014239, 1.9992946087893353)

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The sample mean and variance approach those of the distribution, here 1/2 and 1/4:

#% cell
seed(4); xs = random_variate(exponential_distribution(2), 10^4); [mean(xs), variance(xs)]
#% output
#= [0.49959193150953823, 0.24694037843684094]

#% cell
[mean(exponential_distribution(2)), variance(exponential_distribution(2))]
#% output
#= [1/2, 1/4]

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A distribution with a symbolic parameter cannot be sampled:

#% cell
random_variate(normal_distribution(mu, 1))
#% output
#! failure(argument, random_variate, "the parameters of the distribution must be numeric")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `seed`, `normal_distribution`, `random_real`, `random_normal`, `histogram`, `estimated_distribution`
